{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question","id":1498108,"title":"MtA/M20 Magic question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-26T20:05:31-08:00","id":1498108,"title":"MtA/M20 Magic question","content":"We have an ongoing debate at the table trying to decide at what point does a spell (or the effects of a spell) become permanent? I know that with 6+ successes a spell can become permanent with Storyteller option. At what point do spells that heal, spells that create or alter something, when do they become permanent?<br /> <br /> - Does a healing spell from Life 2 or 3 end and your wounds open back up?<br /> - If I turn a vampire into a lawn chair, does he revert to normal at the end, or does the spell end and the results of the spell remain?<br /> - If I make a stone wall using Prime and Matter, does the wall stay a wall at the end of the spell?<br /> <br /> What spells are permanent without 6 successes, and which spells need those 6 successes?<br /> <br /> Please help.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27594-ingeloak","name":"Ingeloak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T00:46:53-08:00","id":1498115,"title":"","content":"There is no simple answer, because the game is purposefully vague/flexible so that the ST can ensure the free form magic system stays within the tone they're aiming for.<br /> <br /> That said, in general, when a spell &quot;ends&quot; the impact of the spell doesn't go away. If I throw a fireball, the fireball disappears when the spell ends, but anything burnt by it, or set on fire in the process, doesn't have that revert. The fireball ceases to exist, but the burns it caused still happened, so need to be healed. If I turn a broken piece of steel into clay, and then remold it back into it's proper pre-broken shape, when it reverts back to steel it will be in that form.<br /> <br /> Basically, everything that happens during of duration of the spell doesn't get retconned out of the timeline because the spell ends. Permanent (or at least long duration) spells are when you need the spell itself to keep on going. A ward isn't much use if the spell ends before any intruders try getting into your Sanctum. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T02:39:02-08:00","id":1498120,"title":"","content":"Permanence means one of two things in Ascension. There permanent as in \u201cindefinite duration\u201d and then there\u2019s permanent as in \u201cmagic that will last forever\u201d<br /> <br /> Indefinite duration is when you pump 6 successes into an effect. The effect is essentially permanent with a few caveats.<br /> 1. If the effect is vulgar then it may succumb to the effects of unbelief if witnessed by enough sleepers. While no ruleset is provided for unbelief, a common house rule is that the effect loses a few successes, either becoming weaker or losing duration. Very much up to the ST how that plays out.<br /> 2. Duration length is up to ST discretion. 6 successes is just the threshold for indefinite duration. In theory the ST can declare that adding to duration like this only extends and effect for a year or so, this makes it essentially permanent all intents and purposes since there are precious few chronicles that span multiple years, but it isn\u2019t generation spanning. Alternatively the ST might decide a little Time magic is required to push duration of an effect beyond the 6 month threshold, even allowing duration to shift towards the timelines chart after the initial 6 successes is reached.<br /> 3. Your Focus can make indefinite duration a pain. If your focus requires active concentration such as via psychic telekinesis, maintaining a mental link, maintaining a prime sword, etc, then it will add to your active effects limit, with difficulty for casting other stuff given a +1 per 2 active effects. Furthermore having 2 active effects locks you out from conducting rituals, which severely limits the kinds of indefinite duration effects you can create.<br /> If your Focus instead externalises the magic such as machines to keep an eye on people, prayer to god to allow good fortune, or placing a thought in someone\u2019s head that you don\u2019t need to maintain, then concentration is not required until the duration of the spell expires, at which point it will start to contribute to your simultaneous effect limit. The same goes for effects locked in to patterns with matter/life/forces<br /> <br /> True permanence requires the creation of a wonder, and that is done with prime. This makes an effect which essentially casts itself so you don\u2019t have to. At a base level, this can be done by using Prime to invest quintessence in to your effect and then using Prime 3 to make the effect ongoing but only for as long as it is charged with quint (possibly requiring a periapt to be rechargeable, or to keep feeding it tass) or Prime 4 to make it truly permanent (so even if it runs out of quint, it will still run when topped up later).<br /> These effects become a) immune to unbelief, vulgar or not, b) not subject to your or your paradigm, so they\u2019ll function regardless of whether or not you are standing in the room.<br /> <br /> Magic which involves damage, giving or removing, tends to be instantaneous. You cast the effect and the damage is transferred or removed, and that is the end of it. This includes matter effects made to destroy or repair matter patterns.<br /> <br /> Effects to transform, however, are based on duration, so transforming a human (or non-human) into an object or animal will be subject to duration as would using matter to turn lead in to gold.<br /> <br /> Life effects can be made permanent without prime by accepting flaws or applying experience points to the change, and similarly Matter effects to change their shape and form can be made permanent through application of craft. The exception of this is effect which enforce a change of state to a matter pattern, such as changing water in to ice or brick walls in to smoke, which can only be permanent upon achieving mastery with Matter alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T11:40:23-08:00","id":1498144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question?p=1498115#post1498115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no simple answer, because the game is purposefully vague/flexible so that the ST can ensure the free form magic system stays within the tone they're aiming for.<br /> <br /> That said, in general, when a spell &quot;ends&quot; the impact of the spell doesn't go away. If I throw a fireball, the fireball disappears when the spell ends, but anything burnt by it, or set on fire in the process, doesn't have that revert. The fireball ceases to exist, but the burns it caused still happened, so need to be healed. If I turn a broken piece of steel into clay, and then remold it back into it's proper pre-broken shape, when it reverts back to steel it will be in that form.<br /> <br /> Basically, everything that happens during of duration of the spell doesn't get retconned out of the timeline because the spell ends. Permanent (or at least long duration) spells are when you need the spell itself to keep on going. A ward isn't much use if the spell ends before any intruders try getting into your Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the clay revert to steel? My thought would be the spell turns something into clay, then ends. If you want steel again, cast another spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27594-ingeloak","name":"Ingeloak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T12:25:28-08:00","id":1498152,"title":"","content":"Mage, generally speaking, relies on the concept of &quot;Patterns.&quot; Everything has a baseline Pattern unique to itself. Magic that overrides Patterns reverts as the Pattern tries to reassert itself (this can be violent enough to theoretically be used to kill someone if the magic is vulgar)..<br /> <br /> The Pattern of the bar is to be steel, once the magic making it something not-steel ends, the Pattern wants to be steel again. Mage treats Matter Patterns as easier to alter than Life Patterns for various reasons, so access to direct Pattern alteration instead of form alteration is easier with Matter, but that's not exactly what you're asking about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T01:42:03-08:00","id":1499042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ingeloak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question#post1498108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Does a healing spell from Life 2 or 3 end and your wounds open back up?</div> </div> </div> </div>A healing spell dont &quot;end&quot; anymore than a wounding spell gets &quot;unwounded&quot; once the effect &quot;ends&quot;.<br /> <br /> Healing and wounding is always permanent (or at least until the body is healed/wounded back again, naturally or not). You need 1 success to affect a target besides yourself, and each success besides that heals 2 levels of damage. There's no time limit on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ingeloak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question#post1498108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If I turn a vampire into a lawn chair, does he revert to normal at the end, or does the spell end and the results of the spell remain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire reverts back to normal after the spell's end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ingeloak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question#post1498108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If I make a stone wall using Prime and Matter, does the wall stay a wall at the end of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wall gets dispersed back again into the Ether, which cannot be collected and is lost (much like energy that ends up dissipated in the form of heat)<br /> <br /> Think of it this way: a material object created from the Ether (Quintessence) without enough successes to &quot;make it stable&quot; (turn it permanent), is too unstable in its &quot;ethereal fluctuations&quot;, and thus after the time passes upon which your spell bound that locus of Ether into that solid form, without the power of your spell bounding that Ether into that specific solid form, it simply dissipates back into the Ether - and lets not forget, the Ether (or Quintessence) is like heat, it is present everywhere and dissipates in the environment. And like heat, once it dissipates, it cant be easily captured. Thus, after the spell ends, that point (or points) of Quint you spent into making the wall, is lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 12-07-2022, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T02:21:11-08:00","id":1499044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ingeloak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question#post1498108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have an ongoing debate at the table trying to decide at what point does a spell (or the effects of a spell) become permanent? I know that with 6+ successes a spell can become permanent with Storyteller option. At what point do spells that heal, spells that create or alter something, when do they become permanent?<br /> <br /> - Does a healing spell from Life 2 or 3 end and your wounds open back up?<br /> - If I turn a vampire into a lawn chair, does he revert to normal at the end, or does the spell end and the results of the spell remain?<br /> - If I make a stone wall using Prime and Matter, does the wall stay a wall at the end of the spell?<br /> <br /> What spells are permanent without 6 successes, and which spells need those 6 successes?<br /> <br /> Please help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that is exactly the reason why transformations are temporary, but repair/damage spells are permanent. It's because of the Pattern. When you heal a living being using Life or mend a broken object using Matter, you are &quot;Restoring the Pattern&quot; of that being or object; thus the restored state becomes the new Pattern of the subject of the spell. Likewise, it's the same reason of why damage spells are also permanent (to either living beings or inanimate objects). Once you break a glass, its broken state becomes its new Pattern.<br /> <br /> Transformations however, are temporary because they are a deviation of the Pattern of the subject. That's why the clay bars revert back to steel.<br /> <br /> And that's EXACTLY what means to &quot;turn an effect permanent&quot;: it means literally to CHANGE THE PATTERN OF THE SUBJECT.<br /> <br /> That holds true even for Wonders too: when you place a &quot;magick effect&quot; on an object (or living being) using Prime (3, 4 or 5, depending on what is being done), what you are actually doing is &quot;weaving&quot; the ethereal patterns of the subject. I believe something like this is even explained under Prime Sphere, at least for Revised Edition.<br /> <br /> To better visualize it: when you create a Wonder, you are playing with the &quot;ethereal wave-lenghts&quot; of the subject. If you think for a moment in electromagnetism, everything has electromagnetic energy, and that has a wave lenght. Change the parameters of that wave and you change the electromagnetic energy of anything.<br /> <br /> If we think in this similarly to Ether, we could say that changing the &quot;ether-wave&quot; changes the primordial functions of the object. So lets throw in some more technobabble into it, just to illustrate: &quot;if you wanna create a *scepter of healing*, you need to change the object's Ether Pattern to a 231 nn ether-wave. Oak pieces of wood normally have a ether-wave of 287 nn, so you must adjust your modulator to reduce it precisely by 56 nn&quot;.<br /> <br /> The reason for this technobabble example is to illustrate how the creation of Wonders of any kind is nothing more nothing less than the manipulation of the Ethereal Patterns of an object (or living being using Prime 5 rather than 4). You permanently changes the Ethereal Pattern of the object (but the Material Pattern remains the same - a sword remains a sword, a rabbit remains a rabbit, but now they are &quot;magick&quot; because their Ether fluctuations have been permanently altered).<br /> <br /> I hope that with this illustration, the Prime Sphere also becomes more clear (since it's the second hardest sphere to understand)<br /> <br /> EDIT: by the way, once you turn a transformation permanent, that becomes the &quot;New Pattern&quot; of the subject of the spell, which means that this new form is what the subject will henceforth return to. For example, if you permanently change the sex of a person, that becomes their new Pattern; lets for example say that you turn a man into a woman permanently. If another mage tries to &quot;revert back&quot; and turn the now woman back into a man, the subject will simply revert into a woman after this new spell ends, because the subject's Pattern has being permanently changed (thus it would require to do another permanent change to &quot;revert back&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 12-07-2022, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T08:34:37-08:00","id":1500038,"title":"","content":"Quick question, guys and girls.<br /> Can a mage with Arete 3 or lower cast a spell without his usual focus? Maybe if he's experiencing a critical situation without any time to perform his usual rites for the magik?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T08:57:46-08:00","id":1500042,"title":"","content":"So, to the basics of the question asked, yes: Working Without Focus is detailed on page 566 of M20 core. That said technomancers can't access this option.<br /> <br /> It's worth reading the next section on Working with Unfamiliar Instruments, which is far less punishing than trying to override Focus in general with pure will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T06:19:49-08:00","id":1500093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question?p=1500042#post1500042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to the basics of the question asked, yes: Working Without Focus is detailed on page 566 of M20 core. That said technomancers can't access this option.<br /> <br /> It's worth reading the next section on Working with Unfamiliar Instruments, which is far less punishing than trying to override Focus in general with pure will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That are ways to sort of &quot;circumvent&quot; that limitation for technomancers, in limited ways. Of sorts.<br /> <br /> For instance, instead of using your &quot;crazy-scientist brain-improving helmets of Ether&quot; as your technomancer Focus for Mind 1 to improve your mental traits, you could have &quot;Military Training&quot; or &quot;Self Hypnosis&quot; as the focus, and instead of using your silly hat filled with funny lights, you close your eyes for a few seconds in meditation, perhaps using some sort of mental conditioning (like singing small songs to remember a formula for your math test), and that's it. It could work for Entropy 1 too.<br /> <br /> But that's not exactly doing a procedure without any toys, but rather doing a procedure that uses mental conditioning as a focus instead of needing some weird device","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T05:09:38-08:00","id":1500367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question?p=1500038#post1500038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, guys and girls.<br /> Can a mage with Arete 3 or lower cast a spell without his usual focus? Maybe if he's experiencing a critical situation without any time to perform his usual rites for the magik?</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting without the usual focus, action, or actvity can a choice or an option in many situations or on various occasions. Lack of Foci, insufficient preparations, being at the height of particular emotions, extreme duress or hardship (it has to be noted that hardships do not have to be a negative factor or circumstance), a bout of being carefree, extreme need or desire for spontanous choices and actions can all lead to unusual casting decisions and methods.<br /> <br /> I would that casting without usual / regular focus and methods usually can occur in situations during which a Magi / Wizard / Mage encounters and fails to deal, or cannot handle, difficulities in regard to some phenomena or factors:<br /> <br /> 1) The environment, including of course traversing and travel through an level / region / area<br /> <br /> 2) Material belonging, personal items, and the use of resources<br /> <br /> 3) Strict and direct personal limitations - emotions, tendencies in choices, mood, attitude<br /> <br /> 4) Involvement of other supernatural characters, perhaps especially from groups that the Mage has not been up to date with; or is for this or that reason(s) not familiar with. A Wizard / Magi / Mage can from time to time make major or serious errors / mistakes in regard to planning, decisions, and also various possible problems during interactions and situations.<br /> <br /> Such problems / difficulties in regard to the mentioned / described circumstances can lead to differences and radical approaches in regard to achieving / casting Magick Effects. But it has to be noted that events can happen differently then from what it might seem at first, and that personal choices and decisions, and the values behind them, can shine very brightly even in troublesome or difficult situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T10:50:50-08:00","id":1500381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1498108-mta-m20-magic-question?p=1500367#post1500367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would that casting without usual / regular focus and methods usually can occur in situations during which a Magi / Wizard / Mage encounters and fails to deal, or cannot handle, difficulities in regard to some phenomena or factors:</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like you're over complicating things here. This is all fairly well covered in M20 between the magical difficulty modifier chart, and the aforementioned Working Without Focus and Working with Unfamiliar Instruments sections. Plus a few Merits and Flaws out there if you want to give some mechanical oomph to your character's magical style being heavily based on various things (ex: Conditional Magic).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}